config MTK_RAM_CONSOLE
	bool "MediaTek RAM console (last-kmsg via pstore/ramoops)"
	depends on PSTORE_RAM
	depends on MTK_AEE_IPANIC
	default n
	help
	  Enables the MediaTek RAM console driver for the Dimensity 7030
	  (MT6879) platform.  The driver:

	    * Exposes the previous boot's kernel console log as
	      /proc/last_kmsg so that Android init and bug-report tools
	      can retrieve it early in boot.

	    * Reads the bootloader's "ram_console" property from the
	      /chosen device-tree node (if present) and makes the SRAM/DRAM
	      log region available for inspection alongside the standard
	      pstore/ramoops interface (/sys/fs/pstore/).

	  The persistent write path is provided by aee_sram_printk() from
	  the MTK AEE/mrdump subsystem (CONFIG_MTK_AEE_IPANIC).  pstore RAM
	  backend (CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM) and the ramoops DTS node at 0x48000000
	  provide the cross-reboot console log retention.

	  Say Y here to enable debugging of custom-kernel boot failures.
	  If unsure, say N.
